In article <1993Jan28.203703.5499@llyene.jpl.nasa.gov> robert@triton.Jpl.Nasa.Gov (Angelino) writes:

>I know DEC has OSF 1 running on Decs and Alphas.  I'm trying to find
> other vendors as well if they exist??

Which are you interested in OSF/DCE or OSF/1?  In the case of OSF/DCE,
you have to specify if you are interested in the DCE RPC portion,
threads, DFS or the whole ball of wax.  Various systems have different
portions.

The DCE RPC, time stuff, threads, etc.  have been ported to a very
wide variety of systems.  The Windows NT SDK includes DCE RPC and
Microsoft claims DCE is the wave of the future.  I believe Gradiant
(Transarc?) and one other vendor have ported DCE to Windows.  HP,
DEC, IBM and a large variety of other workstation vendors have ported
DCE to their workstations.

Availability of the ports differs between the vendors.  The DFS
portion of the DCE is taking longer, but should be available in the
next couple of quarters.

regards,
fletcher
